<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sejo of Joseon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1417–1468</span> · Also known as Grand Prince Suyang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sejo was the seventh king of Joseon, ruling from 1455 to 1468. A son of Sejong, as Grand Prince Suyang he seized power in 1453 from ministers serving his young nephew Danjong and forced him to abdicate in 1455. He executed officials who plotted Danjong's restoration and abolished the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hall-of-worthies">Hall of Worthies</a>. He strengthened royal power and the military, and began the National Code, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyeongguk-daejeon">Gyeongguk daejeon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sejo-of-joseon.jpg" alt="Sejo of Joseon" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 김은호 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EC%84%B8%EC%A1%B0_%EC%96%B4%EC%A7%84_%EC%B4%88%EB%B3%B8.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
